:- module(tc, [foo/1, bar/1, ping/1]).

% X is shared between an int-typed and a string-typed head position.
% HNF splits it into two variables joined by a `GuardEqual`, which is
% an evidence form: ask-equality succeeds only on identical terms, so
% the guard asserts the two positions have the same type. Within the
% typed fragment they never do, so the rule can never fire — dead
% code, YCHR-20104 (a warning), not a type error (see
% docs/reference/type-system.md §Inaccessible branches). The program
% still compiles and runs.
:- chr_constraint foo(int), bar(string), ping(int).

bad @ foo(X), bar(X) <=> true.
live @ ping(R) <=> R = 1.
